    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present 8 Kilmoroney Close - an impeccably presented three bedroom detached home offering contemporary comfort and exceptional energy efficiency. With an impressive A3 BER and a full SEAI deep retrofit completed in 2018 (featured on RTÉ's Eco Eye in 2018), this turnkey property blends style, practicality, and sustainability—ready for its new owners to move straight in.\n\nFront and approach\nNestled in a quiet cul de sac, No. 8 features private off street parking. The tarmac driveway with granite edging and simple flower beds creates a clean, low maintenance aesthetic that complements the home's modern facade.\n\nGround floor\nInside, an inviting hallway with generous under stairs storage leads to a guest WC and a cosy living room—ideal for relaxing and family time—featuring a 4 kW stove for efficient, ambient heat. The spacious, light filled kitchen/dining room forms the heart of the home, enjoying south-facing views of the rear garden. A versatile playroom/home office completes the ground floor. The home is network ready, with CAT5 internet points in each room to support reliable connectivity for work, study, and streaming.\n\nFirst floor\nUpstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms. The master bedroom includes its own ensuite, while a modern family bathroom serves the remaining two bedrooms. Each room is finished to a high standard with ample room for storage.\n\nOutside\n\nTo the front, there is a generous driveway. The suntrap, south facing rear garden is perfect for outdoor dining, play, and unwinding. A practical garage and additional storage provide further flexibility.\n\nEnergy and upgrades\nIn 2018, the property underwent a full deep retrofit via an SEAI pilot programme, achieving its A3 BER. Works included complete rewiring, upgraded roof insulation, solar PV, mechanical ventilation for improved air quality and comfort, and a modern heat pump system—delivering lower running costs, year round comfort, and compliance with contemporary building standards. The retrofit and its outcomes were featured on RTÉ's Eco Eye (2018), highlighting the home as a case study in sustainable upgrades.\n\nLocation\nNo. 8 Kilmoroney Close enjoys a prime Donaghmede location, combining suburban tranquillity with excellent connectivity. Donaghmede Shopping Centre, the local library, swimming pool, and scenic parks are moments away, with villages Raheny, Malahide, and Howth also nearby. Families will benefit from easy walking access to a wide selection of primary and secondary schools.\n\nTransport\nCommuters have superb transport options; frequent H1 and No.15 bus services and Howth Junction & Donaghmede DART station are a short stroll, offering effortless city centre access. The M50, M1, and Dublin Airport are all within easy reach.\n\nWhether you're starting a family, downsizing, or investing, No. 8 offers location, lifestyle, and longterm value. Early viewing is strongly recommended to fully appreciate all this exceptional property offers. Please contact DNG to arrange your viewing.\n\nAccommodation\nGround Floor \nEntrance Hallway L: 3.5 m x W: 2.0 m \nGuest WC L: 2.0m x W: 0.9m \nLiving L: 3.5 m x W: 4.5 m \nKitchen L: 3.6 m x W: 5.6 m \nPlayroom/Office: L:3.4 m x W:2.4 m \nUtility/Garage L: 2.0 m x 2.4W: m \n \nFirst Floor \nFamily Bathroom: 1.9m x W:1.9 m \nBedroom One L: 2.7m x W: 2.4m \nBedroom Two L: 2.8m x W: 3.6m \nBedroom Three L: 3.7m x W: 3.4m"
      },
      {
